CA 6700 is based on SIS 630. Acpi works on it with only "acpi=force" in 
LILO. This is becouce there is two different bioses present. first one 
(version 1.0.012) with date from 1997. The other one is from 2003 (year 
of production) in version 1.18... Linux finds the first one and seeing 
the date turns ACPI of, that can be turned on however. Please dont ask 
my why it is like that. All I can say is that it was that way since 
purchase.

It works, but can not find FAN. I dont know if it is chipset, laptop 
manufacturer or Linux ACPI problem, but maybe you can put some light to 
it, because it works like monster and some speed control to it would be 
just awsome

I attached the required output for linux commands for development purposes.

www.ca.pl -- web site of the manufacturer

http://ftp.ca.pl/pub/ca6700/bios/ca6700t/2xTR118.zip --- bios presently 
used on the laptoop

With regards

Wojciech Myrda

